Proposed diff for _tag_bag -- NOT APPLIED, and NOT RECOMMENDED on this evidence alone.
See the session report for why. Two things matter if it is ever applied:

  1. The threshold MUST move with it. 2/1/3 shrinks the tag bag's similarity scale, so at the
     unchanged 0.80 it simply clusters finer (+29 clusters/run) -- that is a granularity change
     wearing a weighting's name, and it is NOT what was measured. The measured result is at
     matched granularity, which needs CLUSTER_JOIN_THRESHOLD ~0.825.
  2. _TAG_BAG_WEIGHTS must move with it too; the test asserts the pairing.

Measured at matched cluster count over 10 archived runs: junk pairs -2.6pp (9/10 runs),
passengers -6% (7/10), singleton rate -4.1pp. Extraction-noise band 0.6pp; three-regime spread
3.0pp; effect falls to -0.6pp median when the metric's primary_event bias is removed.

--- a/newsroom/src/cluster_extractjoin.py
+++ b/newsroom/src/cluster_extractjoin.py
@@
-_TAG_BAG_WEIGHTS = {"entities": 3, "keywords": 1, "primary_event": 2}
+_TAG_BAG_WEIGHTS = {"entities": 2, "keywords": 1, "primary_event": 3}
@@
 def _tag_bag(tag: dict) -> str:
-    """Term bag for one article: entities x3 (strongest same-story signal), primary_event x2.
+    """Term bag for one article: primary_event x3 (strongest same-story signal), entities x2.
+
+    The x3/x1/x2 this replaces had entities outweighing primary_event 1.5:1, which inverted the
+    blind-judge ranking in docs/2026-07-02-dedup-poc-findings.md (primary_event AUC 0.923,
+    entity-overlap 0.867). Swept over 10 archived runs at matched granularity, moving to 2/1/3
+    cuts junk pairs 2.6pp (9/10 runs) and groups 4.1pp more articles.
+
+    Entity weight is NOT dropped further, and no field is dropped. Entities are the most
+    REPRODUCIBLE field across two independent extractions of the same articles (token Jaccard
+    0.895 vs primary_event's 0.757); zeroing primary_event while entity weight stays high is
+    catastrophic (3/1/0 +6.3pp, 4/1/0 +9.2pp, 1/0/0 +19.7pp); and EVERY single-field ablation
+    loses cohesive pairs (-3.8% to -40.8%), 0/0/1 (primary_event alone) worst at -21.9%.
+    What the sweep actually localises is the RATIO: entities:primary_event above ~1 is worse,
+    and production's 1.5 is the wrong side of it.

     Returns "" when the article has no usable tags -- the caller then substitutes a per-article
     unique token so tagless articles stay singletons instead of collapsing into one junk blob
     (all-identical bags -> cosine distance 0 -> forced merge).
     """
     ents = [e.lower() for e in tag.get("entities", [])]
     kws = [k.lower() for k in tag.get("keywords", [])]
     pe = str(tag.get("primary_event", "")).lower().strip()
-    parts = ents * 3 + kws + ([pe] * 2 if pe else [])
+    parts = ents * 2 + kws + ([pe] * 3 if pe else [])
     return " ".join(p for p in parts if p.strip())

